# --------------------------------------------------
# Git LFS Rules
#
# Git Large File Storage (LFS) stores large file contents on an LFS server
# and small pointer files in Git history. Git LFS filters restore the contents
# in the working tree and upload new objects when pushing.
#
# Contributors must have the Git LFS client installed before working with
# LFS-tracked assets. Rules in this file apply to media/ and its descendants.
# SVG source stays in Git as text and does not require Git LFS.
#
# Configure Git LFS once per clone after installing the client:
# git lfs install --local
# git lfs pull
#
# Common commands:
# Show tracking patterns:           git lfs track
# List tracked LFS files:           git lfs ls-files
# Show pending LFS changes:         git lfs status
# Download and restore files:       git lfs pull
# Download without restoring:       git lfs fetch
# Restore already downloaded files: git lfs checkout
#
# Run these tracking commands from media/, then commit .gitattributes
# together with the assets. Quote patterns to prevent shell expansion:
# git lfs track "*.[pP][sS][dD]"
# git add .gitattributes path/to/asset.psd
#
# Troubleshooting commands:
# Show configuration and endpoint:  git lfs env
# Show the latest LFS error log:    git lfs logs last
# Check local objects and pointers: git lfs fsck
# Check an asset's effective rules: git check-attr filter diff merge text -- path/to/asset.psd
#
# If files contain pointer text instead of asset contents, try git lfs pull.
# git lfs checkout only restores objects already available locally and does
# not overwrite modified files. Check GIT_LFS_SKIP_SMUDGE and fetch include
# or exclude settings if expected files remain pointers.
#
# Missing remote objects require an upload from a clone holding the contents.
# From that clone, git lfs push origin HEAD uploads objects for the current ref.
# Authentication, endpoint, and server quota errors must be resolved before
# retrying the transfer. git lfs fsck can move corrupt local objects to
# .git/lfs/bad and cannot recover contents missing from every copy.
#
# Tracking patterns do not convert existing history. After changing the rules,
# convert the current version of an already tracked asset from media/ with:
# git add --renormalize -- path/to/asset.psd
#
# Use git lfs migrate only when deliberately migrating commits and coordinate
# any history rewrite with collaborators.
# Removing a tracking pattern does not restore historical contents to Git.
#
# CI jobs also need Git LFS configured and the required objects downloaded.
# Existing pre-push hooks must retain the Git LFS upload step. If installation
# reports a hook conflict, get integration guidance with:
# git lfs install --local --manual
#
# For more information, see:
# https://git-lfs.com/
# https://github.com/git-lfs/git-lfs/tree/main/docs/man
# --------------------------------------------------

# --------------------------
# Common Rules
#
# Store binary media formats and asset bundles in Git LFS.
# Keep editable SVG source as normal Git text.
# Patterns also apply to files in subdirectories.
# --------------------------

# Documents
*.[oO][dD][tT]          filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[oO][dD][sS]          filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[oO][dD][pP]          filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[eE][pP][uU][bB]      filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[rR][tT][fF]          filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[dD][oO][cC]          filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[dD][oO][cC][xX]      filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[dD][oO][cC][mM]      filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[pP][dD][fF]          filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[xX][lL][sS]          filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[xX][lL][sS][xX]      filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[xX][lL][sS][mM]      filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[pP][pP][tT]          filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[pP][pP][tT][xX]      filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[pP][pP][tT][mM]      filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# SVG source
*.[sS][vV][gG]          -filter !diff !merge text eol=lf

